WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.392
Damon followed Ivan and Kelsey off the school bus and looked around nervously.

2
00:00:13.393 --> 00:00:17.309
The field was crowded with people in historical costumes.

3
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:22.809
There were women in long dresses and bonnets, and men in straw hats and leather boots.

4
00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:28.437
"Welcome to Pioneer Days!" Mrs. Manning, the teacher, said.

5
00:00:28.438 --> 00:00:34.511
"In the 1800s around 400,000 people left their homes in the East.

6
00:00:34.512 --> 00:00:39.865
They wanted to settle on open land and find new opportunities.

7
00:00:39.866 --> 00:00:46.174
So these pioneers traveled across America in covered wagons to settle in the West."

8
00:00:46.175 --> 00:00:51.131
"What kind of person wants to dress up like a pioneer?" Kelsey said.

9
00:00:51.132 --> 00:00:54.890
"Yeah," Damon mumbled.

10
00:00:54.891 --> 00:01:00.601
He spotted his mother standing by an open fire, wearing her homemade outfit.

11
00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:05.388
Before his friends could notice her, Damon pointed wildly across the field.

12
00:01:05.389 --> 00:01:08.190
"Look at the oxen!"

13
00:01:08.191 --> 00:01:12.371
"Wow!" Ivan stared at the huge animals.

14
00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:15.230
"Why are cows pulling a wagon?

15
00:01:15.231 --> 00:01:17.666
Why not just use horses?"

16
00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:22.184
"They're oxen, not cows, Ivan!" Mrs. Manning said.

17
00:01:22.185 --> 00:01:28.262
"Pioneers used oxen instead of horses to pull wagons because they're strong, tough—"

18
00:01:28.263 --> 00:01:34.339
"And slow!" Kelsey giggled as the oxen trudged past.

19
00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:39.034
"See the cream pail on the side of the wagon?" Mrs. Manning said.

20
00:01:39.035 --> 00:01:43.187
"The wagon's motion churns the cream into butter."

21
00:01:43.188 --> 00:01:48.138
Damon noticed Mom waving at him, but he pretended not to see.

22
00:01:48.139 --> 00:01:52.881
"Let's go learn about the Native Americans!" he said hurriedly.

23
00:01:52.882 --> 00:01:55.344
Mrs. Manning checked the time.

24
00:01:55.345 --> 00:01:56.807
"It's lunchtime now.

25
00:01:56.808 --> 00:02:10.201
We're having an authentic pioneer lunch!"

26
00:02:10.202 --> 00:02:15.223
"Shouldn't we see the cow-milking station first?" Damon asked hopefully.

27
00:02:15.224 --> 00:02:19.796
"After lunch," Mrs. Manning said firmly.

28
00:02:19.797 --> 00:02:22.422
"Damon!" Kelsey said suddenly.

29
00:02:22.423 --> 00:02:24.864
"Isn't that your mom?"

30
00:02:24.865 --> 00:02:29.248
Damon wished he could disappear.

31
00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:35.071
"Hello, everyone!" Mom smiled cheerfully as she handed out plates of food.

32
00:02:35.072 --> 00:02:39.887
"Everything you're eating here was cooked over an open fire.

33
00:02:39.888 --> 00:02:43.853
Most pioneers didn't pack their heavy stoves in the wagons.

34
00:02:43.854 --> 00:02:47.364
So they cooked in iron pots called Dutch ovens."

35
00:02:47.365 --> 00:02:50.528
She gestured at the pots by the fire.

36
00:02:50.529 --> 00:02:55.056
"They baked bread and biscuits in these, and cooked beans and stews.

37
00:02:55.057 --> 00:03:01.905
They had to pack enough flour, beans, rice, cornmeal, and bacon for six months of hard traveling.

38
00:03:01.906 --> 00:03:07.816
Sometimes they had to clean the bacon before they ate it, to remove mold or bugs."

39
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:10.830
"Moldy bacon?" Kelsey said.

40
00:03:10.831 --> 00:03:15.353
"Bugs? Yuck!" Ivan pretended to throw up.

41
00:03:15.354 --> 00:03:18.190
"Moldy bacon was the least of their worries!"

42
00:03:18.191 --> 00:03:20.989
Damon suddenly heard himself say.

43
00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:25.645
"The pioneers had to survive storms and diseases.

44
00:03:25.646 --> 00:03:30.293
They turned their wagons into boats to float across flooded rivers.

45
00:03:30.294 --> 00:03:34.907
Sometimes they even lowered them down cliffs on ropes.

46
00:03:34.908 --> 00:03:39.734
When they finally settled, they could only use what they had brought with them!

47
00:03:39.735 --> 00:03:45.961
They had to build their own houses, grow their own food, and make their own clothes.

48
00:03:45.962 --> 00:03:48.462
Nothing was easy for them!"

49
00:03:48.463 --> 00:03:51.039
His friends blinked at him in surprise.

50
00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.944
Damon flushed.

51
00:03:52.945 --> 00:03:55.929
Now they were really going to tease him!

52
00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:59.498
"Wow!" Kelsey said finally.

53
00:03:59.499 --> 00:04:02.959
"I guess the pioneers were pretty tough."

54
00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.375
"And smart," Ivan said.

55
00:04:06.376 --> 00:04:08.975
"How do you know all this, Damon?"

56
00:04:08.976 --> 00:04:13.969
"My mom brings me to Pioneer Days every year," Damon admitted.

57
00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:17.368
"I guess I've learned a few things!"

58
00:04:17.369 --> 00:04:24.346
"These biscuits are delicious!" Kelsey said with her mouth full.

59
00:04:24.347 --> 00:04:26.563
"Can you show me how to make them?"

60
00:04:26.564 --> 00:04:31.469
Maybe seeing Mom in her pioneer outfit was not so bad after all.

61
00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.947
"Sure." Damon grinned.

62
00:04:33.948 --> 00:04:40.447
"But only if you dress up like a pioneer!"

